      "id": "summary",
      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Study reveals that pesticide poisoning kills 11,000 people each year, with India accounting for nearly 60% of fatalities</p><p>Almost half of the world’s farmers are poisoned by pesticides every single year, a <a href=\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/public-health/articles/10.3389/fpubh.2026.1825899/abstract\">study</a> has found.</p><p>Using publicly available data from 2006-2023, the study, which was commissioned by <a href=\"https://www.pan-uk.org/\">Pesticide Action Network</a>, found there to be an estimated 402-433m cases of unintentional acute pesticide poisoning of farmers and farm workers every year.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/sep/02/50-per-cent-world-farmers-poisoned-pesticides-every-year-experts\">Continue reading...</a>"
